# BuildTwin Frontend

Paths resolve from the repository root. Read `AGENTS.md` and the canonical constitution at
`../buildtwin/.specify/memory/constitution.md` before work. Backend: `../buildtwin`, port `8080`.

## Data flow

UI components consume **domain models** from `src/features/domain/models/`, never `src/types/api/` DTOs directly. Mappers live in `src/features/domain/mappers/`.

## API integration

- Browser calls `/api/v1/*` (Next.js rewrite → `BUILDTWIN_API_URL`)
- Server Components fetch `BUILDTWIN_API_URL` directly

## OrthomosaicResolver

Pages depend on `OrthomosaicResolver` interface only. Historical default guidance names
`MockOrthomosaicResolver` with demo mappings; this does not establish commercial validity.
Verify real API retrieval and authorization in commercial journeys, including API failure cases.

## Demo mode

**Conflict identified:** historical offline/default-demo guidance can hide real API or auth failures.
Demo assets such as `/demo/orthomosaic-preview.jpg` belong only to isolated, labeled demo checks.
Commercial acceptance requires demo disabled, real authentication, and explicit failure states.
Do not change app behavior or weaken tests merely to satisfy historical demo assumptions.
The existing Playwright config starts a mock API; its success is not real-stack acceptance.

## Logo

Run `npm run prepare:brand` after updating `~/Downloads/buildTwin.png`. Uses original brand colors with transparent background — do not invert colors.

## CSP (next.config.ts)

- Dev: `unsafe-inline` + `unsafe-eval` + `ws:` (React/Turbopack HMR)
- Prod: no `unsafe-eval`

## Forbidden

`any`, `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`, `eval` in app code, direct DOM manipulation.
